[Music]  hey guys i'm chef joya and i'm an expert  at transitioning non-vegans to vegan  food today we're making vegan southern  fried chicken  maple collards and candy yams using five  ingredients or less let's go ahead and  get started  so we're gonna start off by heating our  oil and we're using grapeseed oil for  this recipe we're gonna add that to the  pot so for my southern fried chicken we  are going to use oyster mushrooms i  absolutely love oyster mushrooms because  it has a very meaty texture now you want  to make sure that you clean your  mushrooms with a towel you don't want to  put these in water because it will  absorb it and your mushrooms will become  mushy now the chicken can be any size  that you want we're going to have some  that smaller pieces so all you have to  do is break them up right at the base  and you want to keep that base intact  because that's going to hold your  mushroom together so i'm going to use  poultry seasoning because it has all of  the herbs and spices you need so we're  going to get that mixed in the bowl this  is going to just taste amazing it's not  going to take like fried mushrooms  because all of the seasonings is going  to taste just like fried chicken so  we're going to take half of our seasoned  flour and we're going to add this into a  shallow pan because we're going to need  a wet and a dry batter so for our wet  batter we're going to add our club soda  to our seasoned flour and we're going to  whisk that in there so we want it to be  about the texture of pancake batter  because it is going to thicken up over  time i love the club soda because it  gives the chicken extra crispy and a  lighter texture so we're going to put it  into our dry batter and we're going to  give that a nice little coat so we're  going to take our chicken pieces and put  it in our wet batter and once we get  those coated evenly we're going to put  it back in our dry batter so now that we  have our oil nice and hot and our  chicken pieces have been fully covered  we're going to add this to the pan now  we want to start with our bigger pieces  first because it takes longer to cook  now you want to get as many chicken  pieces that you can get in the pan  without overcrowding the pan because i  will slow down the process of your  cooking your vegan chicken  and just like with anything it'll make  it really oily and you don't want that  we want this to be light and crispy  all right so we're going to turn over  our first piece of chicken  like if you don't tell anybody they  wouldn't even know that it's vegan like  it looks just like fried chicken so we  got all our pieces turned we're going to  let that cook for about another two  minutes all right and it should be nice  and golden brown and we're going to use  the paper towel so we can drain any  excess oil this looks absolutely  delicious i cannot believe that i got  this recipe down to five ingredients all  right let's get into this chicken  this is absolutely delicious like look  at this you can give this to somebody  that's not vegan it looks like meat do  you see this do you see this like matter  of fact don't even when you make this  don't even tell people that it's vegan  chicken make sure they don't have a  mushroom allergy though please  let's go ahead and get started on our  other sides  all right let's start by heating our oil  in a pan and next we're going to add our  onion and we're going to slice them so  you can slice them or dice them it's  just whatever your preference is all  right so we're going to add our onions  to the oil so this is going to cook down  for about three minutes so your onions  are almost translucent and then we're  going to add our collard greens so i add  half of my collard greens to the pan and  i'm going to go ahead and mix that  around so let's go ahead and get that  cooked down and then we're going to add  the remaining half so we have this first  half almost covered with our infused oil  and onions and we're going to add our  remaining collard greens to the pen any  time i cook collard greens it reminds me  of my mom collard greens is my one of my  mom's cooking staples she's known for  her collard greens in wisconsin she's  won every competitions that she competed  in my mom even ships me collard greens  to north carolina hey mama don't forget  this year so once we get these coated  all the way we're going to go ahead and  add our seasonings the vegan bouillon  i'm going to use you'll find at the  asian market so let's go ahead and get  that mixed in there and then next we're  going to go ahead and add our seasoning  i like to use an all-purpose seasoning  so i'm going to add that to my pot and  give that a nice stir now i haven't  added any water to the pan but you can  see that there is water that's coming  out because the greens is going to  release the water but i do add a little  bit more and we're going to turn this on  high and once it starts to boil we're  going to change it to simmer and let it  cook for 30 minutes this is 2 pounds of  calories you wouldn't think that but  it's not going to cook down like spinach  [Music]  now that our collard greens are done to  our desired tenderness it is time to add  our maple syrup i started using maple  syrup instead of sugar because it gives  it more of a robust flavor so now that  our greens are done we're going to go  ahead and put it in our bowl and we're  gonna get all of the liquid in the  bottom of our pot that is called the pot  liquor i can't have greens without the  pot liquor okay so we have our maple  collards  ready to go and it's time to give it a  taste  test this is real good even if you cook  collard greens with meat there is  absolutely no need to this is the  perfect collard green recipe for any day  we're going to start off with our peeled  candy yams and we're going to slice them  about a half inch thick and we're gonna  use about four to five medium to large  whatever you prefer now that we have our  yams in a bowl we're gonna mix in our  seasonings so we're gonna take our brown  sugar and then we're gonna use our  cinnamon sugar now this is one of my  cheats and my tips because you can buy  the cinnamon and sugar already mixed  together next we're going to add our  vanilla extract next we're going to use  our vegan butter now you can use  whatever kind of vegan butter you want  you can use a coconut base avocado base  whatever vegan butter you want you just  want to make sure it does not overpower  your dish we're going to mix this all up  you want to make sure that every potato  gets covered in our sugar and butter  mixture we're going to put this right  into our aluminum pan you can use a  glass pan if you want to it just takes a  longer cook time once we put it into our  aluminum pan it's going to help  caramelize the potatoes and it's going  to be absolutely delicious once we get  that spread out into an even layer we're  going to top it with some aluminum foil  i'm going to make sure we have it sealed  up real nice  oh yeah baby oh yeah oh  look at that  [Music]  like this is like big mama house this is  home there you have it we have made our  vegan thanksgiving with five ingredients  we have our southern fried chicken our  maple collards and candy yams i would  love for you to try these recipes at  home so make sure you tag me at  cookingwithjoya and let me know what you  think happy thanksgiving from my family  to yours see you next time ciao  oh yes  [Music]  you

